      "message": "[error] Line 167: 🔴 An authenticated peer\u0027s `clock` is accepted without a bound. A linked device (or a crafted imported state) can advertise `UINT64_MAX`; the next local update then hits clock exhaustion permanently, turning one metadata merge into an account-wide write DoS. Reject states that cannot support a subsequent local revision, or define a saturating/recovery policy before persisting the remote clock.",
