      "message": "[error] Line 243: 🔴 The destination has already been renamed before the parent-directory `fsync` is attempted. If this `fsync` fails, the method reports failure while the new state may already be visible on disk, but the in-memory `state_` remains unchanged; subsequent reads and syncs return the old snapshot and a later update can overwrite the committed state with stale data. Reconcile/reload the state after a post-rename failure (or otherwise make the store unusable until recovery) so the reported failure cannot leave divergent in-memory and on-disk state.",
      "revId": "1d3a1dd54bf08d92099fa2c06c6f13be0bea5da7",
