      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T10:45:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 16-bit limit is per multiplexed frame, not per SyncMsg. Bundled dhtnet ChannelSocket::write (src/channel_socket.cpp:454-474) already fragments size_t writes into \u003c\u003dUINT16_MAX frames; the persistent buildMsgpackReader reconstructs the byte stream. sbuffer(UINT16_MAX) is initial capacity, not a cap. PS2 clarifies the stale comment and adds actual production-reader regressions at serialized sizes 65534/65535/65536 plus store-validated near-4MiB metadata across split and coalesced chunk patterns, for current and legacy readers; malformed input is rejected. The 13-test serializer suite passes. No extra fragmentation protocol or lower storage limit is necessary. These are reader regressions, not a claim of end-to-end 4MiB TLS testing.",
